Proposition 4.2 says the order on \(D_\infty\) is coordinatewise. `inverseLimitLE` is that relation, reducible to the pointwise inequality. `inverseLimitLE_refl`, `inverseLimitLE_trans`, and `inverseLimitLE_antisymm` are reflexivity, transitivity, and antisymmetry, each proved at a single coordinate and reassembled. The partial-order instance that stores them is on the [limit lattice](1972_Limit_lattice.md) note. **Theorem:** yes — the coordinatewise order and its three laws are formalized. **Proof:** no — the relation is an abbreviation. The three laws are proved.
